PROGRAM reserve stock with explicit rejection

RECORD Stock
  available: integer

RECORD Order
  quantity: integer

REQUEST reserve stock
  GIVEN stock is Stock
  GIVEN order is Order
  WHEN reserve order from stock
  OUTPUT stock is Stock

WHEN reserve <order> from <stock>
  GIVEN order is Order
  AND stock is Stock
  REQUIRE order.quantity > 0
  print "checking stock"
  REQUIRE stock.available >= order.quantity
  subtract order.quantity from stock.available
  print "reserved"

SCENARIO insufficient stock rejects without reserving
GIVEN stock is Stock
  available: 2
AND order is Order
  quantity: 3

REQUEST reserve stock
THEN fails with "assertion_failed"
AND stock.available == 2
AND prints ["checking stock"]

SCENARIO valid order reserves its quantity
GIVEN stock is Stock
  available: 3
AND order is Order
  quantity: 2

REQUEST reserve stock

THEN stock.available == 1
AND prints ["checking stock", "reserved"]

SCENARIO nonpositive quantity rejects before checking stock
GIVEN stock is Stock
  available: 3
AND order is Order
  quantity: <quantity>

REQUEST reserve stock
THEN fails with "assertion_failed"
AND stock.available == 3
AND prints []

EXAMPLES
  | quantity |
  | 0        |
  | -1       |
